# Part 2 — The pseudoreplication problem {-}

# Ignoring blocks and subplots

Fit a linear model of yield with nitrogen and variety as predictors, using all 72 strips, and print the summary. Then make a new data frame with one row per subplot (each block × variety combination, with its mean yield), fit a linear model of mean yield against variety, and print its summary.

```{r pseudoreplication}

